This seems to say that the name of a letter can not be used to refer to the=
 letter but that such a reference requires longer expression. =A0This is in=
herently implausible, since a name is, by definition, used to refer to the =
thing named. =A0That it may also be used for other things does not obviate =
this primary function; it just means you have to be careful. =A0The written=
 form is particularly tricky, since the theory seems

to be that the letter can be anaphoric, not the name of the letter, though =
the conventions do not distinguish well under the isomorphism.

